{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ugh. our ADK travel agent has a `book_hotel` tool that POSTs to the partner booking API, and that API randomly hangs for 30s+ then times out. I wrapped it in tenacity with 3 retries and now QA found two duplicate reservations for the same guest. Partner docs mention an `Idempotency-Key` header but I'm not sure what to key it on: session id? tool call id? Also the confirm step happens in a previous turn (user says 'yes book it'), so how do I make sure the booking fires once even if the agent re-invokes the tool after a Cloud Run restart? Demo is Thursday, please help."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Looking for a design review. We have a payments agent built on Google ADK, deployed to Agent Engine. Flow: the LLM proposes a charge, we surface it to the user for approval via a confirmation event, and only on approval does `charge_card()` call Stripe-like provider (actually an internal gateway, ~2% 504 rate). Requirements from compliance: an approved charge must settle exactly once; a rejected or abandoned one must never hit the gateway, even if the model hallucinates a second tool call later. Currently approval state lives in session.state which feels fragile. What's a sound pattern here (persisting intents in Firestore? an outbox? reconciling ambiguous timeouts by querying the gateway)? Python 3.12, happy to restructure."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "my ADK agent keeps getting 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED from Gemini when a bunch of users hit it at once, the whole tool loop just dies. should I add retries? backoff? where do I even hook that in with the Runner", "needs_instead": "Help handling rate limits/quota on the Gemini model calls themselves (retry/backoff config for the LLM client, quota increases, concurrency limiting), not exactly-once execution of side-effecting external tool calls."}
]}
